    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a periodic dielectric multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate for normal incidence. Use Germanium (Ge) as high-index material and Zinc Sulfide (ZnS) as low-index material. Stack topology: CaF2 | (Ge/ZnS)_8 | Air, totaling exactly 16 finite dielectric layers. Initialize all layers at quarter-wave optical thickness centered at 4.45 μm. Optimize all 16 layer thicknesses to maximize transmittance in two passbands (4.15-4.35 μm and 4.55-4.75 μm) while minimizing transmittance in two stopbands (3.60-4.00 μm and 4.85-5.20 μm). No metal layers. Evaluate at wavelengths 3600-5200 nm. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all valid candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
